# Dependency Ledger

Purpose:
  Continuous security and dependency monitoring triggered on every git push.
  Tracks seen-resolved problems to prevent re-triggering stops for known issues.

Owns: security\DEPENDENCY-LEDGER.sdd

## Monitoring Flow

Trigger: git push

Flow:
  1. Run dependency/security scan (npm audit, go list -u, Dependabot alerts).
  2. IF new problem found:
       → STOP current work regardless of context
       → Focus entirely on this problem
       → Apply fix
       → Run regression test suite
       → ONLY return to previous work after regression passes
       → Record problem in ledger
  3. IF problem already in ledger as RESOLVED:
       → Log as "known, skip"
       → Do NOT stop execution
  4. IF problem not in ledger:
       → Execute step 2 flow

## Ledger Format

Ledger_File: .specdd/dependency-ledger.md

Format:
  | Date       | Problem/CVE               | Status    | Fix commit |
  |------------|---------------------------|-----------|------------|
  | 2026-08-18 | lodash CVE-2026-XXXX      | RESOLVED  | a1b2c3d    |

Fields:
  Date: ISO date of discovery/fix
  Problem/CVE: Issue identifier or CVE ID
  Status: RESOLVED | OPEN | SKIPPED
  Fix_commit: Git commit hash that resolved the issue

## Memory Behavior

Memory:
  - Ledger is the single source of truth for seen problems.
  - RESOLVED entries prevent re-triggering stops.
  - Only NEW (not in ledger) problems trigger full stop-and-fix flow.

State: +
